@startuml
title ai-ddd-devtrack System Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

actor User

package "Frontend\nReact + TypeScript + Vite" as Frontend {
  [Dashboard]
  [Learning Goals UI]
  [Study Sessions UI]
  [Certifications UI]
  [TanStack Query API Client]
}

package "Backend\nSpring Boot" as Backend {
  package "presentation" {
    [REST Controllers]
    [OpenAPI Definition]
  }

  package "application" {
    [Learning Application Services]
    [Certification Application Services]
  }

  package "domain" {
    [Learning Domain Model]
    [Certification Domain Model]
    [Repository Interfaces]
  }

  package "infrastructure" {
    [JPA Persistence Adapters]
    [JPA Entities]
    [Domain-JPA Mappers]
    [Spring Data Repositories]
  }
}

database "PostgreSQL" as PostgreSQL

User --> Frontend
Frontend --> [TanStack Query API Client]
[TanStack Query API Client] --> [REST Controllers] : HTTP JSON
[REST Controllers] --> [Learning Application Services]
[REST Controllers] --> [Certification Application Services]
[Learning Application Services] --> [Learning Domain Model]
[Certification Application Services] --> [Certification Domain Model]
[Learning Application Services] --> [Repository Interfaces]
[Certification Application Services] --> [Repository Interfaces]
[JPA Persistence Adapters] ..|> [Repository Interfaces]
[JPA Persistence Adapters] --> [Domain-JPA Mappers]
[JPA Persistence Adapters] --> [Spring Data Repositories]
[Spring Data Repositories] --> PostgreSQL
[OpenAPI Definition] ..> [TanStack Query API Client] : future generated client

note right of [Learning Domain Model]
Type:
Pure Java domain model

Responsibility:
Represent LearningGoal and StudySession behavior.

Dependencies:
No Spring, JPA, HTTP, or PostgreSQL dependency.

Persistence:
Saved through domain repository interfaces.
end note

note right of [Certification Domain Model]
Type:
Pure Java domain model

Responsibility:
Represent Certification, exam planning, attempts, and results.

Dependencies:
No Spring, JPA, HTTP, or PostgreSQL dependency.

Persistence:
Saved through domain repository interfaces.
end note

note bottom of [JPA Persistence Adapters]
Type:
Infrastructure adapter

Responsibility:
Convert between domain models and JPA entities.

Business Rules:
Must not own domain invariants.

Dependencies:
Spring Data JPA and PostgreSQL integration.
end note

@enduml

